/Title (The chart illustrates a highly volatile regulatory landscape, with the probability of the Clarity Act becoming law in 2026 oscillating between 40% and 84%. The dramatic spike to 84% in mid-February followed strong executive endorsements, but was immediately met with a sharp drawdown toward 50% due to Senate gridlock regarding stablecoin yield provisions. However, as of mid-March, odds have stabilized around 60% following the recent bipartisan breakthrough on activity-based rewards. For quantitative analysts, this volatility serves as a "Regulatory Risk Premium" indicator, signaling that while structural breakthroughs are occurring, execution risk remains high heading into the midterm cycle.)
